{"from": "claim:ac-28-26-isaiah-6-9-10-quoted", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-13-14-15-isaiah-6-quoted", "note": "The same passage (Isaiah 6:9-10) quoted again: in Acts 28 by Paul against the Roman Jews; in Matthew 13 by Jesus to the crowds. Same quotation, different speaker and setting."}
{"from": "claim:ac-28-26-isaiah-6-9-10-quoted", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:jn-12-39-40-isaiah-6-10-quoted", "note": "John 12:39-40 cites Isaiah 6:10 for why they could not believe; Acts 28:26-27 quotes verses 9-10 in full as Paul's parting word. Same quotation, different application."}
{"from": "claim:ac-28-31-paul-death-tradition", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:jn-21-18-19-peters-death", "note": "Parallel martyrdom traditions of the two leading apostles in Rome: 1 Clement 5 reports both Peter's and Paul's deaths (see the reused 1 Clement node)."}
