{"from": "text:strabo-geography-6-2", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-28-12-syracuse", "grade": "B", "note": "Strabo, Geog. 6.2 names Syracuse among Sicily's cities and sailing distances ('to Syracuse thirty-six') - the harbour Acts 28:12 puts in at; the three-day stay is Acts-only."}
{"from": "text:strabo-geography-6-2", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-28-13-rhegium", "grade": "B", "note": "Strabo, Geog. 6.2 names Rhegium opposite Messene across the strait - the port Acts 28:13 touches; the arrival itself is Acts-only."}
{"from": "text:seneca-epistle-77", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-28-13-puteoli", "grade": "B", "note": "Seneca, Ep. 77.1 names Puteoli and its docks where the Alexandrian grain ships land - the Campanian port Acts 28:13 reaches; the arrival itself is Acts-only."}
